  "summary": "Fine warp-ikat cloths of Flores where sea-worms, ancestral ships and horses swim through blurred dye.",
  "description": "Flores weavers bind and dye warp threads before looming so that sepaq sea-worms, jade horses, ancestral ships and skull-tree motifs rise through softly feathered ikat edges — the island's signature blur-on-precision. Districts guard their own palettes: Sikka's fine rayon sheen ikats, Ende's deep-earth tones, Lio's ceremonial lawo butu worn at initiation feasts. Cloth remains bride-wealth, mortuary shroud and church-festival finery, and Flores ikat ranks among Indonesia's most collected textiles.",
